message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "scientific-reasoning-auditor"
# Keep `version` in lockstep with pyproject.toml [project].version and
# src/sra/__init__.py __version__.
version: 0.7.0
authors:
  - name: "Furox-Art"
    email: "furkanarkn1451@gmail.com"
abstract: >-
  Evidence-traceable screening and reasoning review for scientific manuscripts.
  Audits the chain from hypothesis through assumptions, methods, data, analysis
  and inference to conclusion, and reports reviewable reasoning risks with
  evidence locations and reproducibility metadata. Includes academic-writing and
  citation checks, discipline evidence adjudication, DOI and PMC validation,
  arithmetic verification of reported Welch t-tests and two-proportion z-tests,
  a reasoning graph with strict validation, source-bound semantic-review
  templates for external models, and reproducibility provenance. Emits review
  signals rather than verdicts and does not declare a manuscript scientifically
  true or false.
license: MIT
